  "id": "d22e810a-efea-44be-a4f1-0d16b923b27e",
  "title": "Peaceful protests are fundamental rights, but credentials matter in Delhi",
  "summary": "The Bombay High Court has ordered the Maharashtra government to address allegations of illegal detention of protesters during anti-CEC demonstrations, emphasizing that while peaceful protests are a fundamental right, their credibility and public inconvenience must be considered before blanket restrictions on police action. The court has also ruled in favor of advocates who sought to prevent police from detaining individuals participating in peaceful demonstrations in Delhi.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Bombay High Court directed the Maharashtra government to respond to petitions alleging illegal detention of protesters during anti-CEC demonstrations in Delhi.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court ordered the police not to detain individuals taking part in peaceful protests, citing the need to weigh credentials and public inconvenience.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Advocate Gayatri Singh submitted an application in support of this ruling, citing public interest litigation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
